# Citation metadata for REEL-QUEST. GitHub renders this as "Cite this repository".
# `doi` is the Zenodo record of v1.0.0 (reserved 2026-10-30); add ORCIDs when known.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use REEL-QUEST, please cite it as below. Please also cite the
  papers that reported any specific measurements you rely on (each
  condition's reference.DOI).
type: software
title: >-
  REEL-QUEST: A Digital Platform for Exploration of Rare-Earth Extraction
  Ligands and Quantitative Understanding of Elemental Selectivity Trends
abstract: >-
  A curated, structure-keyed database of liquid-liquid extraction
  distribution ratios for the lanthanides (La-Lu) plus Y and Sc, with
  per-measurement provenance, a 21-subtype SMARTS taxonomy of extractants,
  per-ligand selectivity-trend classification across the lanthanide series
  with bootstrap confidence intervals, a Python API, a read-only REST API
  and an interactive dashboard.
